  "least_like_the_real_thing": [
    "Latency is fitted from very little: 5 sequential calls per model, tiny answers, one time of day, one client location (Groq region 'bom'). The spread (sigma) and the prompt-size slope are rough; there is no measured tail, no diurnal change, and no network jitter beyond what the fitted header delay already contains.",
    "No concurrency knee was measured: every real call was sequential. The knee and the slowdown per extra request are assumptions, so the stand-in's behaviour under load is a design input, not a calibration.",
    "Failure behaviour is invented. Groq returned 0 errors in 16 calls, so 5xx rates, stragglers and stalled streams are scenario settings, not measured rates.",
    "No 429 was ever observed on Groq. The 429 body wording, the retry-after value and whether Groq rejects (rather than queues) at a limit follow the documentation and the client's parser, not evidence.",
    "Token accounting differs. Groq's remaining-tokens drop did not equal the reported usage; the stand-in reserves prompt + max_completion_tokens at admission and gives back the unused part at the end. The real rule is unknown, and the token-bucket reading of reset-tokens failed for some calls (see header_checks).",
    "RPM and TPD are not known. Groq exposes neither in headers; the stand-in enforces them only when an experiment sets a value, labelled as a scenario setting.",
    "Groq keeps separate limit counters per model (each model restarted at 999). The stand-in keeps one set of buckets for all models.",
    "Answers are extractive copies of passage sentences, at most two sentences. Real answers are longer and paraphrased, so output length, output tokens per answer and the time spent streaming content are not like Groq's. Output tokenisation (4 characters per token) is assumed.",
    "Reasoning is a fixed number of filler tokens per model (the measured median). Real reasoning length varies with the question and can use most of the token budget.",
    "Prompt tokenisation was fitted on synthetic probe prompts, not on paper text with equations and identifiers, which usually tokenises into more tokens per character.",
    "Streaming granularity differs: one SSE chunk per word with an even inter-token gap. Groq batches tokens into chunks of varying size."
  ],
